The magnetic force on a moving charge is given by:
\vec{F} = q(\vec{v} \times \vec{B})
Given:
q = 1 \mu C = 1 \times 10^{-6} C
\vec{v} = (\hat{i}-2\hat{j}+3\hat{k}) \text{ m/s}
\vec{B} = (2\hat{i}+3\hat{j}-5\hat{k}) \text{ T}
First, calculate the cross product \(\vec{v} \times \vec{B}\):
\vec{v} \times \vec{B} = \begin{vmatrix} \hat{i} & \hat{j} & \hat{k} \\ 1 & -2 & 3 \\ 2 & 3 & -5 \end{vmatrix}
= \hat{i}((-2)(-5) - (3)(3)) - \hat{j}((1)(-5) - (3)(2)) + \hat{k}((1)(3) - (-2)(2))
= \hat{i}(10 - 9) - \hat{j}(-5 - 6) + \hat{k}(3 + 4)
= \hat{i}(1) - \hat{j}(-11) + \hat{k}(7)
= \hat{i} + 11\hat{j} + 7\hat{k}
Now, substitute this into the force equation:
\vec{F} = (1 \times 10^{-6}) (\hat{i} + 11\hat{j} + 7\hat{k}) \text{ N}
The magnitude of the force \(|\vec{F}|\) is:
|\vec{F}| = (1 \times 10^{-6}) \sqrt{1^2 + 11^2 + 7^2}
= (1 \times 10^{-6}) \sqrt{1 + 121 + 49}
= (1 \times 10^{-6}) \sqrt{171} \text{ N}
We are given that the magnitude of the force is \(\sqrt{\alpha} \times 10^{-6}\) N. Comparing this with our result:
\sqrt{\alpha} \times 10^{-6} = \sqrt{171} \times 10^{-6}
\sqrt{\alpha} = \sqrt{171}
\therefore \alpha = 171

The potential energy of a magnetic dipole in a uniform magnetic field is given by:
U = -\vec{M} \cdot \vec{B}
The most stable position is when the magnetic moment is aligned with the magnetic field (\(\theta = 0^{\circ}\)), so \(U_{\text{stable}} = -MB\cos(0^{\circ}) = -MB\).
The most unstable position is when the magnetic moment is anti-aligned with the magnetic field (\(\theta = 180^{\circ}\)), so \(U_{\text{unstable}} = -MB\cos(180^{\circ}) = -MB(-1) = MB\).
The work done in rotating the magnet from the most stable to the most unstable position is the change in potential energy:
\Delta U = U_{\text{unstable}} - U_{\text{stable}} = MB - (-MB) = 2MB
Given:
• Magnetic moment \(M = 0.5\) Am\(^{2}\)
• Magnetic field \(B = 8 \times 10^{-2}\) T
Substitute the values into the equation for \(\Delta U\):
\Delta U = 2 \times 0.5 \times 8 \times 10^{-2}
\Delta U = 1 \times 8 \times 10^{-2}
\Delta U = 8 \times 10^{-2}\text{ J}

